note TWIN of unroll-nest.om with every unroll removed (section 4 line 91): same expected stdout.
note Contract section 4 lines 87-92 and 105: nested unrolled loops, 8 x 8 = 64 copies of the inner body
note with i and j bound to constants; the folded index add mul i 8 j into the 64-element array m is a
note constant in range (no error 21). Removing unroll (twin unroll-nest-rolled.om) changes nothing.
note Expected stdout: oracle/s3s4/exp/unroll-nest.out (python3, oracle/s3s4/oracle.py).
om2
fn main to int
m = new ulong 64 0
f = ulong 14695981039346656037
for i ulong 8
for j ulong 8
f = mul xor f add mul i 8 j 1099511628211
put m add mul i 8 j add mul i 1000 j
end
end
pu f
g = ulong 0
for k ulong 64
g = add mul g 3 get m k
end
pu g
ret 0
end
